{
  "_why": [
    "THE BOARD IS THE PROPS, and this is the proof of it. One document: `storyboard_check` gates",
    "this file and `npx remotion render Dispatch --props=examples/board.json` renders this file.",
    "They used to be two documents that nothing converted between, so every divergence rule was",
    "being enforced against a board that was not the film.",
    "",
    "It is a real board rather than a fixture. The story is variable-rate irrigation over the",
    "Ogallala, which is the second-ranked beat in knowledge/texas/APPLICATIONS.md and the one the",
    "engine could not draw at all until the agriculture module existed.",
    "",
    "NOTHING HERE IS A PUBLISHABLE CLAIM. There is no numeral in any super or caption, because a",
    "published number traces to a fetched source and a computed value and this file has neither.",
    "A run replaces the copy with its own, sourced."
  ],
  "runtime_s": 40,
  "title": "One machine, a different answer every acre",
  "beat": "farm-ranch-water",
  "derived_from": "scratch",
  "divergence_note": "Built from the pivot outward rather than from a landscape inward. The camera lives UNDER the machine looking up through the span for most of the film, the movement is the sweep of the circle rather than a traverse across it, and the turn is a cut to the ground in section where the water actually is. No prior board has stood beneath anything.",
